at-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",subtoc:"basic",order:51,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is an SLO? Why SLOs Matter for Software Teams",summary:"Learn what SLOs, or service-level objectives, are and why they matter in software reliability engineering. This article explains the differences between SLI, SLO, and SLA, and why teams should use percentiles such as P50, P95, and P99 instead of relying only on averages when measuring reliability."}],g=[{title:"Before Building Claude Code, Boris Cherny Lived in Nara Making Miso",date:"2026-07-16",lastmod:"2026-07-16",toc:"career-talk",lang:"en",fileName:"boris-cherny-before-claude-code",filePath:"src/pages/en/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code.md",fullPath:"/en/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code",subtoc:"career-thinking",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Before Building Claude Code, Boris Cherny Lived in Nara Making Miso",summary:"Before joining Anthropic, Claude Code creator Boris Cherny lived in Nara while working fully remotely as a principal engineer at Instagram. By returning to hands-on coding, delegating leadership, and embracing asynchronous communication, he expanded his impact far from Silicon Valley and learned from miso making to build Claude Code with a longer time horizon."},{title:"Different Career Paths for Engineers in the AI Era",date:"2026-07-02",lastmod:"2026-07-02",toc:"career-talk",lang:"en",fileName:"engineer-career-paths-ai-era",filePath:"src/pages/en/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era.md",fullPath:"/en/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era",subtoc:"career-advancement",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Different Career Paths for Engineers in the AI Era",summary:"Boris Cherny, the creator of Claude Code, observed that as AI reshapes how teams work, roles are starting to blur beyond the old engineering, product, and design boundaries. The five archetypes he describes can help teams understand what kind of people they need at each product stage, but individual engineers should be careful not to let those labels limit their growth."},{title:"Cursor VP of Engineering on Writing Resumes That Actually Get Seen",date:"2026-05-12",lastmod:"2026-05-12",toc:"job-hunting",lang:"en",fileName:"cursor-vp-resume-tips",filePath:"src/pages/en/career/cursor-vp-resume-tips.md",fullPath:"/en/career/cursor-vp-resume-tips",subtoc:"resume",order:31,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Cursor 工程副總談，如何寫履歷讓求職申請更容易被看見",summary:"Based on reviewing hundreds of recent applications, Cursor VP of Engineering Lee Robinson shared practical advice for making engineering resumes stand out. This article breaks down his recommendations on one-page resumes, portfolio and GitHub quality, role-specific tailoring, and clearly showing AI workflow experience."}],c=[{title:"How to Use AI Without Losing Your Technical Judgment",date:"2026-06-12",lastmod:"2026-06-12",toc:"ai-engineering",lang:"en",fileName:"avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",filePath:"src/pages/en/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment.md",fullPath:"/en/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",subtoc:"ai-with-engineer",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How to Use AI Without Losing Your Technical Judgment",summary:"AI agents can make engineering teams faster, but over-reliance can lead to cognitive surrender: accepting AI output without understanding or verification. This article explains the risk through research and real-world examples, then offers practical mechanisms such as pre-commit quizzes, human sign-off, and accountable review practices."},{title:"Use Agent Skills to Scale Staff-Engineer Thinking Across Your Team",date:"2026-04-19",lastmod:"2026-04-19",toc:"ai-engineering",lang:"en",fileName:"agent-skills-staff-engineer-mindset",filePath:"src/pages/en/ai/agent-skills-staff-engineer-mindset.md",fullPath:"/en/ai/